object_copies_generic.vlt:25:11: error: a value of type `AB` converts to `A` by copying its fields, and this program compares `A` values with `===`: two copies of one object are not `===`
object_copies_generic.vlt:26:15: here, or in the function this calls
  = note: TypeScript allows this and passes the same object; Velt's object types have fixed layouts, so the `A` made from a `AB` value is a new object with the same field values
